    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"i statements\" thing feels a bit too soft though... like i'm just expressing an opinion instead of stating a fact. the truth is, they didn't just \"water it down,\" they actively intercepted the trajectory i set. i have the original stems and the early demo tapes from 2016 that prove i was pioneering this before the industry even knew what to call it. it's not just about feelings, it's about the theft of an entire sonic architecture. i want to draft something more powerful than just \"i feel.\" i want to write something that pieces together the timeline and shows people that the current leaders of this genre are just echoes of what i actually built. can you help me structure a kind of manifesto? something that asserts my role as the progenitor?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
